    {
      "id": "grammar-el-la-los-las-que-the-one",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "el/la/los/las + que + descripción",
      "questionEn": "How do you say ‘the one who…’ or ‘the ones that…’ without repeating the noun?",
      "answerEn": "Use el que, la que, los que, or las que to match the unnamed person or thing, then add what identifies it.",
      "noteEn": "Choose el, la, los, or las to show whether the omitted person or thing is masculine or feminine, singular or plural. Que stays unchanged and introduces the identifying description, which normally contains a verb. Each plus sign in the prompt means ‘followed by.’",
      "example": {
        "es": "Ana es la que prepara el café.",
        "en": "Ana is the one who makes the coffee."
